s trust and safety solutions, such as monitoring, reviewing and managing user and advertiser-generated content on online platforms to ensure it complies with community guidelines, legal regulations, platform specific policies, risk management, compliance, identity management and fraud; and artificial intelligence (AI) solutions that consist of data labeling, annotation, context relevance, and transcription services for training and tuning machine learning algorithms that enables to develop AI systems. It serves clients in various industry segments comprising social media, e-commerce, gaming, streaming media, food delivery and ride sharing, technology, financial services, and healthcare. The company was formerly known as TU TopCo, Inc. and changed its name to TaskUs, Inc. in December 2020. TaskUs, Inc. was founded in 2008 and is headquartered in New Braunfels, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Bryce  Maddock | Co-Founder, CEO & Chairman | Age 38 | Compensation: $300,885 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 65K people. Revenue per employee of $18K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers, improving at 12%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $1K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $453 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 17\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["TaskUs, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $833M market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +4.8pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $74M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.34\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 7.6\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 23% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 61% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 65% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"TaskUs (TASK) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/taskus-task-q3-2026-earnings-172826000.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793900677.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"TaskUs (NASDAQ:TASK) Shares Gap Up After Earnings Beat","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/taskus-nasdaqtask-shares-gap-up-after-earnings-beat.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793893971.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.852,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"TaskUs forecasts full-year 2026 revenue of $1.249B-$1.251B while targeting 19% adjusted EBITDA margin (NASDAQ:TASK)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4666176-taskus-forecasts-full-year-2026-revenue-of-1_249b-1_251b-while-targeting-19-percent-adjusted","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793855815.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"TaskUs Inc (TASK) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Record Revenue and AI Services Momentum ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/taskus-inc-task-q3-2026-051328840.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793855608.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.421,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"TaskUs Non-GAAP EPS of $0.34 beats by $0.03, revenue of $314.7M beats by $11.41M (NAS